_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Require a current head SHA for current CodeRabbit states.**

Line 766 falls back to review timestamps when `currentHeadOid` is null. Line 777 accepts any marked request when `currentHeadOid` is null. The classifier can then return `reviewed` or `requested` without an exact head match. This violates the exact-head closeout contract and can suppress a required closeout request.

Require `currentHeadOid` before either current-state branch. Compare normalized review and current head SHAs. Add a regression case with no current head SHA.

